# Cursor Workflow Rules

## Work sequence
1. Understand requirement and identify impacted files.
2. Implement smallest correct change first.
3. Verify with build/tests/lint for touched scope.
4. Summarize what changed and what remains.

## Editing guidelines
- Keep changes scoped to the requested task.
- Do not rewrite unrelated code.
- Preserve user-authored changes when present.
- Add brief comments only where logic is non-obvious.

## Quality checks
- Run lint/checks after substantive edits.
- Prefer fixing root causes over suppressing warnings.
- Verify offline-critical flows when touching data or session logic.

## Documentation discipline
- Update relevant docs in `docs/` when scope/architecture/flow changes.
- Keep implementation aligned with SRS and compliance documents.

## Git hygiene
- Make atomic commits when asked to commit.
- Use clear commit messages focused on why.
- Avoid destructive git operations unless explicitly requested.

## Product guardrail reminder
- Do not introduce cloud-only dependencies for core functionality.
- Maintain fast, accessible, and low-friction shopping flows.
